{
  "manufacturer": "Seneca",
  "manufacturer_slug": "seneca",
  "model": "R-4AO-8DIDO Ethernet I/O (4 analog outputs, 8 digital I/O)",
  "model_slug": "r-4ao-8dido",
  "short_model": "R-4AO-8DIDO",
  "aliases": [
    "R4AO8DIDO",
    "R-4AO-8DIDO",
    "Seneca R series 4AO"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Sensor (remote I/O module, analog outputs)",
  "applies_to": "R-4AO-8DIDO in the Series R I/O manual MI-00604-29-EN.",
  "summary": "The R-4AO-8DIDO is a Seneca R-series remote I/O with four voltage/current analog outputs and eight digital channels that can each be an input or an output, plus eight 32-bit counters. It serves Modbus TCP on a two-port Ethernet switch and Modbus RTU on RS-485. This map covers integer output setpoints, status, digital I/O, counters, period/frequency and the command register.",
  "transport": [
    "TCP",
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 1,
    "baud": 38400,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": 502
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "Modicon",
    "note": "Holding-register tables print the 4x number (40001) and the 0-based offset (0); coils print 1 / offset 0 and discrete inputs 10001 / offset 0. The offset is the wire address."
  },
  "default_word_order": "ABCD",
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "Series R I/O with protocol - User Manual",
    "doc_number": "MI-00604-29-EN",
    "revision_date": "2026-09-03",
    "url": "https://www.seneca.it/media/6848135/mi00604-29-en.pdf",
    "pages": "Modbus conventions pp. 95-100; R-4AO-8DIDO tables pp. 198-202; defaults in the web-server chapter pp. 64-72"
  },
  "notes": [
    "The protocol page lists function codes 01, 03, 05, 06, 15 and 16; the tables also give the digital inputs as 1x input status read with function 02. Modbus RTU runs on RS-485 and Modbus TCP serves up to 8 clients.",
    "Counters, period and frequency rows are printed MSW at the lower address (ABCD). The float analog output setpoints (40072-40079) carry no MSW/LSW marks and the manual has no general word-order rule (a sibling model in the same manual is LSW first), so they are left out; use the signed 16-bit setpoints at 40080-40083 instead.",
    "Factory settings from the manual: static IP 192.168.90.101/24, gateway 192.168.90.1, Modbus TCP port 502, station address 1; RS-485 38400 baud, 8 data bits, no parity, 1 stop bit, address 1.",
    "RW* registers are stored in flash and survive about 10,000 writes.",
    "Analog output values are in engineering units set by the configured scale (default mV or uA); the manual does not give a fixed scale.",
    "Left out: the auxiliary command registers 40013-40016, whose codes are not described, and reserved registers."
  ],
